course: dictionary
lesson: 11765
title: A word from the farm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A barnyard is the yard around a barn on a farm, where animals walk about and find their food. «The hens and ducks scratched in the barnyard, looking for seeds.» The clues are hens, ducks and scratched. Those animals live on a farm, so the barnyard must be the farm yard where they are.
explain: Barnyard can also describe something, so it is an adjective. «The barnyard noises woke us at dawn: moos, oinks and clucks.» Barnyard noises are the sounds that farm animals make.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in "farm" or "farm animals" and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Barnyard is a noun (a barnyard, barnyards) and an adjective.
fact: «Barnyard» means the yard or area around a barn on a farm, where animals walk and feed.
fact: «Barnyard animals» means farm animals such as cows, pigs, hens and ducks.
fact: As an adjective, «barnyard» can also mean rough and rude, as in «barnyard humour».
fact: Phrases to notice: «in the barnyard», «barnyard noises», «barnyard animals».
exercise: «The hens pecked at corn in the barnyard.» Where were the hens? | Up a tall tree | In a shop | *In the barnyard | In a swimming pool
exercise: Which of these is a barnyard animal? | *A pig | A lion | A shark
exercise: «The barnyard noises woke us at dawn.» What were the noises? | Waves crashing on the beach | Traffic and sirens | *Moos, oinks and clucks from farm animals
test: «We sang a song about the cows in the barnyard.» What is a barnyard? | *The yard around a barn on a farm | A type of hat | A small bird | A kind of farm animal
test: Which phrase is about farm animals? | Rainy day | Sandy beach | *Barnyard animals | Snow angels
exam: Jamal says, «That joke was pure barnyard!» What might he mean? | *Rough and rude | Sad and quiet | Very clean and polite | About the sea
